{"name":"Smitten","hex":"#c84186","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smitten","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Affected by an act of smiting.\n\nMade irrationally enthusiastic.\n\nIn love.","Made irrationally enthusiastic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of smite."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smitten"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infatuation","blocks":[{"text":"Infatuation refers to being in love or intensely love smitten, with possible connotations of youth, irrationality, foolishness, or capriciousness. An individual may be considered infatuated with a person they do not know well yet, or whom others view as unsuitable. In the triangular theory of love, \"infatuation\" refers to romantic passion in the absence of intimacy or commitment, as in love at first sight and limerence. A simple infatuation which is more short-lived may be referred to as a crush, or \"puppy love\" in adolescence. Infatuation might also be compared to the \"honeymoon phase\" of a relationship."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infatuation","wikidata":"Q1320124"},{"title":"Smitten (The Martinis album)","blocks":[{"text":"Smitten is the second studio album by American alternative rock band The Martinis. It was released on May 4, 2004 by Cooking Vinyl, remaining as the band's final studio album release."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Martinis_smitten_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smitten_(The_Martinis_album)","wikidata":"Q7545719"},{"title":"Smitten (Pale Waves album)","blocks":[{"text":"Smitten is the fourth studio album by the English rock band Pale Waves. It was released on 27 September 2024 by the independent record label Dirty Hit. Co-produced by Simon Oscroft, Iain Berryman, and Hugo Silvani, Smitten was recorded in both Los Angeles and London, with production beginning in late 2023. Unlike the band's previous albums Who Am I? (2021) and Unwanted (2022), Smitten is closer in style to the group's earlier jangle-inspired synth-pop sound."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a0/Smitten_-_Pale_Waves-Album.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smitten_(Pale_Waves_album)","wikidata":"Q126923260"},{"title":"Smitten (Buffalo Tom album)","blocks":[{"text":"Smitten is the sixth album by Buffalo Tom. It was their only album for Polydor Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/Smitten_%28Buffalo_Tom_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smitten_(Buffalo_Tom_album)","wikidata":"Q7545717"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Kacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_%2846248441824%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKacey_Musgraves_-_Palace_Theatre_St._Paul_(46248441824)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/The_Cranberries_en_Barcelona_13.jpg/500px-The_Cranberries_en_Barcelona_13.jpg?utm_so